---
interface Props {
  data: {
    name: string;
    site?: string;
  };
}
const { data } = Astro.props;
const testflight = data.site ?? 'https://testflight.apple.com/join/1RdVtffd';
---

<div class="ps-page ur-page">
  <nav class="ps-subnav" aria-label="Unroll sections">
    <a href="#top" class="ps-brand" aria-label="Unroll home">
      <strong>Unroll</strong>
    </a>
    <span class="ps-subnav-links">
      <a href="#detection">Detection</a>
      <a href="#evidence">Evidence</a>
      <a href="#modes">Delivery</a>
      <a href="#status">Status</a>
    </span>
  </nav>

  <section id="top" class="ps-hero ur-hero" aria-labelledby="unroll-title">
    <div class="ps-hero-copy">
      <p class="ps-eyebrow"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> Private beta &middot; iOS app</p>
      <h1 id="unroll-title">The ad break, already gone.</h1>
      <p class="ps-lede">
        Unroll finds sponsor reads inside a podcast episode and removes them before you hear them.
        The app runs the whole pipeline on-device &mdash; no account, nothing uploaded.
      </p>
      <div class="ps-actions">
        <a class="ps-btn ps-primary" href={testflight} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join the TestFlight</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ps-release-note">
        Measured across 52 episodes and 55.9 hours, including eight episodes annotated after the
        detector was frozen.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="ur-hero-stats" aria-label="Headline detection results: 95.9% of ads removed, no false cuts, no show audio lost, 55.9 hours evaluated.">
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Ads removed</dt><dd>95.9<small>%</small></dd></div>
        <div><dt>False cuts</dt><dd>0</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Show audio lost</dt><dd>0.0<small>s</small></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Audio evaluated</dt><dd>55.9<small>h</small></dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="detection" class="ps-section ur-detection" aria-labelledby="ur-detection-title">
    <div class="ps-section-head">
      <p class="ps-index">01 / Detection</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="ur-detection-title">A cascade, with a gate at the end.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Not one model asked to be clever. Cheap, specific signals first, then progressively more
        expensive ones, and a strict versioned policy gate before anything is cut.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="ur-cascade">
      <li>
        <span>01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Known fingerprints</h3>
          <p>Recurring sponsor audio and show-specific cue templates match the ads a show runs every episode.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Splice candidates</h3>
          <p>Loudness, silence, VAD and transition analysis find the joins where an insertion sits.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Transcript segmentation</h3>
          <p>Sponsor and advertisement phrasing in the transcript, corroborated against the audio signals above.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>04</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Policy gate</h3>
          <p>A strict, versioned rule decides cut, skip, or pass through. Uncertain segments survive intact.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="ur-rule">
      <strong>Automatic or pass-through.</strong> A listener never reviews or approves an episode to
      get a usable feed. When evidence is thin, the episode plays whole and the diagnostics are
      recorded &mdash; a passed-through ad costs far less than a wrong cut.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="evidence" class="ps-section ur-evidence" aria-labelledby="ur-evidence-title">
    <div class="ps-section-head">
      <p class="ps-index">02 / Evidence</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="ur-evidence-title">Numbers that survived auditing.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Detection is evaluated across a hand-annotated corpus, not sampled from convenient
        episodes, and the tests that produce these figures are versioned with the detector.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="ur-evidence-grid">
      <article>
        <h3>33</h3>
        <p>hand-annotated episodes across five corpora, including eight built and annotated after the detector was frozen.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>19</h3>
        <p>unannotated episodes reserved for false-positive auditing, so precision is checked against audio nobody tuned on.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>52</h3>
        <p>episodes and 55.9 hours in the evaluation set, with the guards that produce each figure checked in.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>4&times;</h3>
        <p>distinct ways this project previously produced a meaningless detection number &mdash; each documented, so the failure cannot quietly return.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="modes" class="ps-section ur-modes" aria-labelledby="ur-modes-title">
    <div class="ps-section-head">
      <p class="ps-index">03 / Delivery</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="ur-modes-title">Keep your podcast app, or take a small one.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        One analysis core, two ways to deliver it. Neither asks the listener to manage the result.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="ur-mode-grid">
      <article class="ur-mode">
        <p class="ps-index">Proxy feed</p>
        <h3>Your existing app</h3>
        <p>A rewritten RSS feed plus rendered audio with accepted intervals removed. Works with Overcast, Pocket Casts, Apple Podcasts and Audiobookshelf &mdash; anything that accepts a custom feed.</p>
        <p class="ur-mode-caveat">The same-Wi-Fi server is still a one-episode probe. If a player fetches from its own servers instead of the device, the LAN URL is unreachable &mdash; documented, not hidden.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ur-mode ur-mode-player">
        <p class="ps-index">Simple player</p>
        <h3>A narrow first-party app</h3>
        <p>Original audio plus persisted skip zones, with one-tap undo. Nothing destructive happens to the file, so a medium-confidence interval can be surfaced without committing to a cut.</p>
        <p class="ur-mode-caveat">Deliberately not a feature-complete podcast platform. It plays, skips, and gets out of the way.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="status" class="ps-section ur-status" aria-labelledby="ur-status-title">
    <div class="ur-status-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="ps-index">04 / Status</p>
        <h2 id="ur-status-title">What is verified, and what is not.</h2>
        <p>
          The native iOS app is the product and it runs; the build-status notes in the repository are
          the authority on what has actually been exercised. Episode summaries, topics and action
          items run through Apple Intelligence on-device and fail closed to empty fields when
          unavailable. Discovery uses Apple Podcasts and publisher RSS, so no extra credentials are
          involved.
        </p>
        <p>
          A frozen Python implementation stays in the repository as the behaviour contract the Swift
          port is tested against, with two deliberate divergences documented rather than quietly
          reconciled.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-actions">
        <a class="ps-btn ps-primary" href={testflight} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join the TestFlight</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
